1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,080
 I feel like this is the fitness industry's version of stolen valor.

2
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:15,280
 I see influencers do this shit all the time.

3
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:19,480
 They get a famous athlete, celebrity or pro bodybuilder to come to their gym.

4
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:25,040
 They put them through one workout, film it, take a picture, post it.

5
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,700
 And suddenly I train pro athletes.

6
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,520
 I train celebrities.

7
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:31,080
 No you fucking don't.

8
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:34,520
 You worked out with a pro athlete once.

9
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:39,800
 There's a huge difference between putting somebody through a workout and actually coaching

10
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:40,800
 them.

11
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:46,800
 Coaching is seeing that person two, three, four days a week for months, years or decades

12
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:47,960
 at a time.

13
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:52,920
 It's knowing when to push them and when to pull back, how to work around injuries, how

14
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:59,700
 to adjust their program when life gets in the way and actually producing measurable results.

15
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,480
 Anyone can make someone tired for an hour.

16
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:06,880
 The real question is, can you make them better over time?

17
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:12,300
 So the next time you're looking to buy a program online or hire a personal trainer, don't ask

18
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,040
 who they've trained.

19
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:16,640
 Ask who they've actually coached.

20
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:19,080
 Thanks for listening to this TED talk.

21
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:26,880
 I'm gonna get back to my workout now.

22
